  "issue_title": "fix(quick-router): fold spoken-word decimals in calculator path (extends #504)",
  "issue_body": "### Summary\n\nPR #504 preserved digit decimals and digit spoken-point forms (`3 point 5` \u2192 `3.5`) in the calculator quick-route, but cardinal-word decimals still fail. The deterministic router feeds `calc_input::prepare` before `calculation_request`, and `fold_spoken_decimals` only folds when the integer and fractional tokens are ASCII digits.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOn `main`, inspect `route()` output for:\n\n- `what is three point five plus two point five`\n- `what is twelve point five percent of 80`\n- `convert ninety eight point six f to celsius`\n\n**Pass (bug present):**\n\n- `what is three point five plus two point five` does not route to `calculate` with expression `3.5 + 2.5`\n- `what is twelve point five percent of 80` does not produce `80 * 12.5 / 100`\n- `convert ninety eight point six f to celsius` does not produce `(98.6 - 32) * 5 / 9`\n\n`what is 3 point 5 plus 2 point 5` works (#504).\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSpoken cardinal decimals fold the same way as digit spoken-point forms:\n\n- `three point five` \u2192 `3.5`\n- `ninety eight point six` \u2192 `98.6`\n- `3 point five` \u2192 `3.5` (mixed digit integer + spoken fraction)\n\nOnly the calculator branch uses `calc_input::prepare`; home/timer/memory routing stays on the integer-only normalizer.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nCardinal words on either side of `point` are left as separate tokens, so percentage, temperature-conversion, and arithmetic extractors never see a decimal token.\n\n### Hardware\n\nJetson (x86_64 dev / cross-build host)\n\n### GenieClaw version / commit\n\n`main` @ current HEAD\n\n### Additional context\n\nNatural extension of #504. Scope is intentionally narrow: fractional part is a single digit word (`zero`\u2013`nine`) or digit token; multi-digit fractional words (`three point one five`) are out of scope.\n",
